# SPEC: 08_entrypoint,65_symbol_clearance
# static-check: off
# Requires: driver
# NEEDS: session
# TIER: T1
# CLEARANCE: 7
# CONSTRUCT: spec/65 F65-26 (corrected 2026-10-17) — an ISOLATED session defines its
#            own symbols freely.  They are local to its fresh context and never reach the
#            host's table; `create_level` only governs adding AT THE HOST.
# COVERS: an own `def` in a restricted session without `create_level`; calling its
#         own creation (possible, because its level IS the clearance, F65-27);
#         no `level:` in the source (that would be self-certification, neg/n16).
# WHY THIS PROBE EXISTS: the draft that used to stand here demanded `create_level` for
#         EVERY definition — and since every aiml program needs a `- def: main` (spec/08),
#         the default 0 would have forbidden every script.  This probe records the correction.
# EXPECT: exit 0.

- def:
    name: my_helper
    return: i32
    body:
      - return: [4]

- def:
    name: main
    return: i32
    body:
      - decl: [got, i32, { call: [my_helper] }]
      - if:
          condition: { neq: [got, 4] }
          then:
            - call: [log.error, "my_helper returned ${got}, expected 4"]
            - return: [1]
      - call: [log.info, "PASS 06 isolated session defines freely"]
      - return: [0]
